## Add Ontology Evolve: check a question, propose a fix, test it before accepting

Context: When a business question cannot be answered, nothing in OntoBricks
says which concept, link or mapping is missing, and a fix can only be
checked after it is saved. Evolve checks a question against a version,
proposes a typed fix with source evidence, builds the parent and the fix
into separate temporary graphs and compares their answers before anything
is saved. Behind `ONTOBRICKS_EVOLUTION_ENABLED` (default off).

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/ontology/evolution/
   Coverage (per-requirement states, join candidates with evidence), rule-based proposal (two new autofix ops), validator, paired evaluation over run-owned graph tables, accept as next DRAFT version.
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/{EvolutionRuns.py,schema.sql,store.py,ReviewEvents.py}
   `evolution_runs` / `evolution_results`; one-transaction accept; review blocked when the design changed after evaluation.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/{BuildPipeline,Builder}.py
   `record_history=False` so evaluation builds never touch the parent's build history.
4. src/api/routers/internal/evolution.py
   `/evolution` routes; Builder role; source probes run as the caller.
5. src/front/…/ontology-evolve.* and menu
   Ontology → Evolve page.
6. tests/units/ontology/evolution, tests/eval, tests/fixtures/evolution
   Unit tests, 30-row dataset, TPC-H fixtures (tiers S/M/L and messy variants).

